{"type":"message","id":"252fca8b","parentId":"d750c427","timestamp":"2026-10-17T22:46:55.858Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py` by replacing `strptime(s, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\")` with `datetime.fromisoformat(s)`. The old format string had no way to match a trailing `Z`, so it raised the error. On Python 3.11 and later (this repo runs 3.13.5), `fromisoformat` understands `Z` and numeric offsets like `+02:00`. `pytest tests/test_parse.py` now passes all 3 tests, including `test_naive` and `test_day_key`.\n\nOne behaviour change: a timestamp ending in `Z` or an offset now comes back timezone-aware (UTC for `Z`). Previously it raised an error, so no working code depended on that. Timestamps without a suffix still come back without a timezone. The only other caller is `day_key`, which just formats the date and isn't affected.\n\nThe risk is mixing the two kinds later: comparing or subtracting a timezone-aware and a timezone-free datetime raises `TypeError`. If anything downstream does that, either convert timezone-aware values to UTC and strip the zone, or make timezone-free values UTC."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":385,"cacheRead":26646,"cacheWrite":461,"totalTokens":27494,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":461}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792277211555,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011Cg8d4DqKBQgH6k57Uvh3b","duration":4297.958784999999,"ttft":4254.1586849999985,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":27109,"nonMessageTokens":21589,"compactionEpoch":0}}}
